---
source: crates/mwf/tests/cli.rs
expression: self.transcript
---
$ mwf show x
[stderr] error[NOT_INITIALIZED]: no .mwf/ directory in [ROOT] or any parent directory
[exit 1]

$ mwf show x --json
{"ok":false,"error":{"code":"NOT_INITIALIZED","message":"no .mwf/ directory in [ROOT] or any parent directory","details":{"start":"[ROOT]"}}}
[exit 1]

$ mwf init
mwf created .mwf/ and added `.mwf/log.md merge=union` to .gitattributes.
Commit .mwf/ and .gitattributes so the team shares the wiki.

Next:
  mwf install --host claude   (or codex, pi, antigravity) so sessions load and save memories
  mwf new <slug> --type <type> --title "..." --summary "..." < body.md
  mwf lint
[exit 0]

$ mwf init --json
{"ok":false,"error":{"code":"ALREADY_INITIALIZED","message":"[ROOT]/.mwf already exists; init changes nothing in an existing project","details":{"path":"[ROOT]/.mwf"}}}
[exit 1]

$ mwf show Not_A_Slug
[stderr] error[INVALID_SLUG]: invalid slug: use one or more of a-z, 0-9 and -
[exit 1]

$ mwf new x --type nonsense --title X --summary x
[stderr] error[INVALID_FIELD]: invalid frontmatter field `type`: must be one of preference, decision, knowledge, incident, task
[exit 1]

$ mwf
[stderr] mwf: a project-local wiki engine for coding agents
[stderr] 
[stderr] Usage: mwf [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
[stderr] 
[stderr] Commands:
[stderr]   init       Create .mwf/ in this git repository root
[stderr]   show       Print a page: frontmatter, body, rev, links out and links in
[stderr]   search     BM25 search over pages; the words of QUERY are joined with spaces
[stderr]   list       List pages by slug
[stderr]   index      Print the table of contents rendered from the current pages
[stderr]   log        Print the last N lines of log.md, oldest first
[stderr]   lint       Check every page; exits 1 when there is an error
[stderr]   new        Create a page; the body is read from stdin
[stderr]   write      Replace a page's body with stdin, if REV is still its rev
[stderr]   patch      Replace the one occurrence of OLD in a page's body with NEW
[stderr]   set        Change frontmatter fields
[stderr]   archive    Set a page's status to archived
[stderr]   unarchive  Set a page's status back to active
[stderr]   rename     Rename a page and rewrite the links to it
[stderr]   delete     Move a page to .mwf/trash/
[stderr]   help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
[stderr] 
[stderr] Options:
[stderr]       --json     Print `{"ok": true, "data": …}` or `{"ok": false, "error": …}` instead of text
[stderr]   -h, --help     Print help
[stderr]   -V, --version  Print version
[stderr] 
[stderr] Host integration (dispatched before the commands above):
[stderr]   install    Add mwf's hooks and skill to a host: mwf install --host <HOST> [--dry-run]
[stderr]   uninstall  Remove them: mwf uninstall --host <HOST> [--dry-run]
[stderr]   hook       Run by the host's hooks, not by hand: mwf hook <event> --host <HOST>
[stderr] <HOST> is claude, codex, pi or antigravity (also agy).
[stderr] `mwf install --help` and `mwf uninstall --help` describe both.
[exit 2]

$ mwf frobnicate
[stderr] error: unrecognized subcommand 'frobnicate'
[stderr] 
[stderr] Usage: mwf [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
[stderr] 
[stderr] For more information, try '--help'.
[exit 2]

